codex
I’ll test a last-layer Gaussian smoothing estimator: run QMC to the penultimate activations, compute sampled mean/variance of the final preactivations, then use the exact ReLU moment of a Gaussian with those moments. This can reduce final ReLU sampling noise if the last preactivation is close to Gaussian.
